    {
        "name": "Uterine Tumor",
        "name_ja": "子宮腫瘍",
        "symptoms": {"vaginal_bleeding", "abdominal_distension", "weight_loss", "appetite_loss"},
        "description": "Uterine Tumor is a neoplastic condition characterized by abnormal cell proliferation that may be benign or malignant.",
        "description_ja": "未避妊メスの子宮の腫瘍。",
        "urgency": "high",
        "recommended_tests": ["ultrasound", "radiography", "biopsy"],
        "causes": "Caused by neoplastic transformation of uterine tissue in intact female hamsters. Hormonal stimulation and chronic endometrial hyperplasia are predisposing factors.",
        "causes_ja": "ハムスターにおける子宮腫瘍の原因: 未避妊メスの子宮の腫瘍。",
        "pathophysiology": "Accumulated genetic mutations lead to uncontrolled cell proliferation, evasion of apoptosis, and potential metastatic spread. Tumor growth causes tissue compression, invasion, and paraneoplastic effects.",
        "pathophysiology_ja": "子宮腫瘍はハムスターにおける腫瘍性疾患である。癌遺伝子、腫瘍抑制遺伝子、DNA修復機構における遺伝子変異の蓄積により腫瘍性形質転換が生じる。制御不能な細胞増殖により腫瘍が形成され、局所組織への浸潤・破壊の可能性がある。悪性腫瘍はリンパ行性または血行性に転移しうる。高カルシウム血症、悪液質、免疫調節障害などの腫瘍随伴症候群が原発腫瘍に伴い、罹患率に寄与することがある。",
        "treatment": "DIAGNOSIS ESSENTIAL (distinguishes tumor type): 1) Abdominal ultrasound—detect uterine mass (hypoechoic, heterogeneous), wall thickening (>3-4 mm abnormal in hamster), assess for rupture (free peritoneal fluid), evaluate both uterine horns bilaterally (tumors often unilateral but 10-15% bilateral). 2) Thoracic radiographs (assess for pulmonary metastasis; 15-25% of uterine tumors have metastatic disease at diagnosis). 3) Abdominal radiographs—assess for peritoneal fluid, evaluate for bone involvement. 4) Blood chemistry panel—assess hepatic/renal function (assess surgical risk given hamster age typically 1.5-2.5 years at presentation). 5) Fine-needle aspirate (if accessible) or histopathology post-excision—confirms tumor type (adenocarcinoma, fibroma, myoma, sarcoma, lymphoma). SURGICAL MANAGEMENT (DEFINITIVE): Ovariohysterectomy (OVE) STRONGLY RECOMMENDED for all hamsters with uterine tumors if metastasis not evident. Complete OVE including BOTH ovaries + entire uterus mandatory (residual tissue = recurrence). PRE-OPERATIVE: blood chemistry, CBC. ANESTHESIA: isoflurane chamber induction PREFERRED (minimizes handling stress on fragile hamster). If injectable: dexmedetomidine 1-2 μg/kg IM (ultra-conservative for 25-150g body weight) + atropine 0.01-0.05 mg/kg SC 10-15 min prior (prevent bradycardia). Temperature strict 32-35°C. SURGICAL TECHNIQUE: tiny ventral midline incision (0.5-1 cm for hamster), careful exteriorization of enlarged uterus/ovaries (VERY FRAGILE—avoid rupture), ligate ovarian/uterine vessels with 6-0 absorbable suture, excise ENTIRE ovaries + uterus (no remnants), close with 5-0/6-0 absorbable sutures. Surgery time <10 minutes CRITICAL (prolonged anesthesia dangerous in hamsters). Send uterus/ovaries for histopathology (tumor type, grade, stage guides prognosis). POST-OPERATIVE: 1) NO FASTING (GI stasis risk). 2) Timothy hay ad libitum IMMEDIATELY. 3) Metoclopramide 0.3 mg/kg SC q24h × 3-5 days. 4) Meloxicam 0.3 mg/kg SC q24h × 3-5 days (short duration due to GI ulcer risk in hamsters). 5) SC fluids LRS 15-20 mL/kg/day × 24-48h. 6) Probiotics (FortiFlora 250 mg/kg/day × 14 days). 7) Monitor appetite hourly first 12h (anorexia = GI stasis). 8) Strict temperature 32-35°C. 9) Suture removal day 7-10. PALLIATIVE CARE (if metastatic or non-surgical candidate due to age/comorbidities): pain management (meloxicam 0.3 mg/kg SC q24h), supportive care (ensure food intake), monitor for hemorrhage from tumor rupture (abdominal distension, lethargy).",
        "treatment_ja": "診断重大（腫瘍型を区別）：1) 腹部超音波—子宮腫瘍検出（低エコー、混合エコー）、壁肥厚（>3-4mm）、破裂評価（遊離液）、両側子宮角評価。2) 胸部X線（肺転移評価；15-25%が診断時転移）。3) 腹部放射線（腹膜液、骨関与評価）。4) 血液化学パネル。5) 穿刺吸引または組織病理—腫瘍型確認（腺癌、線維腫、筋腫、肉腫、リンパ腫）。外科管理（根治）：OVE強く推奨（転移なし時）。両側卵巣+全子宮摘出必須。術前：血液化学、CBC。麻酔：イソフルラン吸入導入推奨。注射時：デクスメデトミジン1-2 μg/kg IM（超保守的）、アトロピン事前。温度32-35°C厳格。外科技術：小型切開（0.5-1cm）、子宮/卵巣外転慎重（FRAGILE—破裂回避）、血管結紮6-0吸収性、全卵巣+子宮切除、閉鎖5-0/6-0吸収性。手術時間<10分重大。組織病理送付。術後：1) 絶食なし。2) チモシーヘイ即座。3) メトクロプラミド0.3 mg/kg SC q24h × 3-5日。4) メロキシカム0.3 mg/kg SC q24h × 3-5日（短期—GI潰瘍リスク）。5) SC輸液 × 24-48h。6) プロバイオティクス × 14日。7) 食欲監視 × 12h。8) 温度32-35°C。9) 抜糸7-10日。姑息的ケア（転移例または高齢/併存疾患で非手術時）：疼痛管理、支持療法。",
        "prevention": "PRIMARY PREVENTION: 1) SPAYING—MOST EFFECTIVE: Ovariohysterectomy before age 1.5 years (uterine tumors extremely rare if spay performed before 18 months; prevents 95%+ of hormone-dependent uterine tumors). Early spaying (6-12 months) OPTIMAL. Late spaying (>18 months) provides some benefit but cannot prevent pre-existing pre-malignant lesions. 2) GENETIC SELECTION (if breeding): avoid breeding females with family history of uterine tumors or early CEH (cystic endometrial hyperplasia). 3) AVOID EXCESSIVE BREEDING (if breeding occurs): retire females by 18-24 months maximum. Limit to 3-4 litters lifetime (each pregnancy cycle increases hormone exposure). 4) ENVIRONMENTAL RISK REDUCTION: avoid cigarette smoke exposure, maintain optimal body weight (25-45g), clean housing. 5) NUTRITION (supportive): vitamin E 20 IU/kg/day (antioxidant), adequate diet; avoid excessive fat. 6) STRESS REDUCTION: minimize handling, 12-hour light-dark cycle, maintain 32-35°C temperature. 7) MONITORING (if breeding/spay delayed): monthly abdominal palpation (detect masses >10 mm if palpable), quarterly ultrasound if retained beyond 12-18 months (assess for pre-malignant changes). 8) EARLY DETECTION: Any vaginal bleeding/discharge in intact hamster >12 months → IMMEDIATE ultrasound (assess for tumor or pre-malignant CEH).",
        "prevention_ja": "一次予防：1) 避妘—最も効果的：OVE 1.5歳前（18ヶ月前に避妘で95%+ホルモン依存性子宮腫瘍予防）。早期避妘（6-12ヶ月）最適。2) 遺伝選別（育種時）：子宮腫瘍またはCEH早期の家族歴回避。3) 過度育種回避（育種時）：18-24ヶ月以内リタイア、生涯3-4産仔。4) 環境リスク低減：喫煙曝露回避、体重最適化（25-45g）。5) 栄養：ビタミンE 20 IU/kg/日、脂肪過剰回避。6) ストレス軽減：明暗周期12時間、温度32-35°C。7) 監視（育種/避妘遅延時）：月1回腹部触診、四半期ごと超音波>12-18ヶ月（前悪性変化評価）。8) 早期発見：膣出血/>12ヶ月未避妘ハムスターで直ちに超音波。",
        "prognosis": "TUMOR-TYPE SPECIFIC OUTCOMES: 1) ADENOCARCINOMA (40-50% of uterine tumors): IF localized (Stage I, no metastasis): 80-90% survival post-OVE (hamster lifespan 2-3 years; may achieve normal remaining lifespan). IF metastatic (Stage II-IV): <30% survival even with surgery (median survival 2-4 weeks post-diagnosis). 2) FIBROMA/MYOMA (30-40%, benign): >95% survival with surgical excision if non-infiltrative. <5% malignant transformation risk. 3) SARCOMA (5-10%, highly malignant): poor prognosis even with surgery (40-50% survival post-OVE); median survival <8 weeks if metastatic. 4) LYMPHOMA (rare): very poor prognosis (<10% survival; chemotherapy rarely pursued in hamsters). STAGE-BASED OUTCOMES: Stage I (tumor confined to uterine wall, no metastasis): 80-90% post-OVE survival. Stage II (invasion beyond serosa, but no distant metastasis): 40-60% survival. Stage III (peritoneal seeding, but no distant visceral metastasis): 20-40% survival. Stage IV (distant metastasis—lungs, liver): <15% survival even with surgery + palliative care. METASTATIC DISEASE (present in 20-30% at diagnosis): Presence of metastasis = SINGLE MOST CRITICAL prognostic factor. 2-year survival drops 70-80% compared to localized disease. Pulmonary metastasis (15-20% of cases) indicates advanced disease (<5% long-term survival). SURGICAL FACTORS: Perioperative mortality 1-3% in healthy hamsters <2 years old. Complete OVE improves prognosis (removes hormone source); does NOT guarantee cure in metastatic disease. POST-OPERATIVE COMPLICATIONS (worsen prognosis): GI stasis (15-25% incidence), hypothermia during/after anesthesia, hemorrhage from incision, dysbiosis from surgery. Each complication reduces survival by 15-25%. AGE AT DIAGNOSIS: Younger hamsters (<18 months) tolerate surgery better (95% surgical completion). Older hamsters (>2 years) have poor tolerance (anesthetic risk 5-10%, comorbidities common). OWNER FACTORS: Post-operative GI stasis prevention compliance CRITICAL—poor compliance = 20-30% worse outcomes. Temperature management during recovery (32-35°C) mandatory. SPAY STATUS: Hamsters spayed before 18 months have essentially ZERO uterine tumor risk. Once tumors develop, cure rates 50-60% lower than if spay had been performed. This emphasizes importance of early spaying (6-12 months optimal prevention). QUALITY OF LIFE post-OVE: excellent if survived (behaviors normalize within 7-14 days, normal remaining lifespan achievable).",
        "prognosis_ja": "腫瘍型別予後：1) 腺癌（40-50%）—限局Stage I で80-90%生存、転移Stage II-IV で<30%（中央値2-4週）。2) 線維腫/筋腫（30-40%、良性）—>95%生存；<5%悪性転化。3) 肉腫（5-10%、高悪性度）—40-50% OVE後、<8週転移時。4) リンパ腫（稀）—<10%。ステージ別：Stage I で80-90%、Stage II で40-60%、Stage III で20-40%、Stage IV（遠隔転移）で<15%。転移疾患（診断時20-30%）=最重要予後因子（生存70-80%低下）。肺転移（15-20%）で高度疾患（<5% 長期）。外科因子：周術期死亡1-3%健全<2歳；完全OVE で予後改善だが転移では治癒保証なし。術後合併症（予後悪化）：GI停滞（15-25%）、低体温、出血、菌叢異常で各15-25%低下。年齢—<18ヶ月好耐性；>2歳で麻酔リスク5-10%。飼主因子—術後GI停滞予防アドヒアランス重大（20-30%悪化）。温度管理必須。避妘状態—18ヶ月前避妘で子宮腫瘍本質的ゼロリスク。腫瘍発生後は治癒率50-60%低下。早期避妘（6-12ヶ月）が最適予防。術後生活品質—優良（行動7-14日で正常化、正常残存寿命達成可）。",
        "onset_pattern": {"chronic"},
        "age_predisposition": {"adult", "senior"},
    },
