    {
        "name": "Dystocia",
        "name_ja": "難産",
        "symptoms": {"straining", "vaginal_bleeding", "lethargy", "abdominal_distension"},
        "description": "Dystocia in hamsters represents prolonged or obstructed labor, a critical emergency requiring immediate intervention.",
        "description_ja": "分娩困難。",
        "urgency": "emergency",
        "recommended_tests": ["radiography", "ultrasound"],
        "causes": "Caused by: 1) Fetal-maternal size mismatch: oversized litters (>8-10 pups), large individual fetuses from long breeding interval; 2) Maternal factors: uterine inertia (inadequate oxytocin sensitivity, calcium deficiency), age (first-time breeders >8-10 months old have 10× higher dystocia risk), obesity (pelvic narrowing); 3) Fetal factors: abnormal presentation (breech, transverse), developmental abnormality (hydrocephalus, anasarca); 4) Environmental: inadequate nesting material, stress, improper temperature (hypothermia suppresses labor).",
        "causes_ja": "ハムスターの難産の原因：胎児-母体サイズ不均合（過大産仔8-10頭以上、長い育種間隔からの大型胎児）。母体因子：子宮無力（オキシトシン感受性低下、カルシウム欠乏）、年齢（初産>8-10ヶ月で難産リスク10倍）、肥満（骨盤狭窄）。胎児因子：異常プレゼンテーション（骨盤位、横位）、発達異常（水頭症、貧血）。環境：産巣材不足、ストレス、不適切温度（低体温で陣痛抑制）。",
        "pathophysiology": "Dystocia in hamsters occurs when uterine contractions (myometrial oxytocin-driven) cannot overcome fetal size, abnormal presentation, or maternal factor (weak contractions). Initial myometrial contractions attempt to move first pup through pelvic canal. If obstruction or inadequate contractions persist >4-6 hours, uterine ischemia develops from sustained tetanic contractions. Prolonged labor (>12 hours total) causes: maternal hypoxemia/acidosis, fetal hypoxia (placental insufficiency from umbilical compression/cord prolapse), uterine rupture, hemorrhage. In hamsters, dystocia rapidly progresses to septic peritonitis/shock due to rapid bacterial translocation and small body size.",
        "pathophysiology_ja": "ハムスターの難産は子宮収縮（筋層のオキシトシン駆動）が胎児サイズ、異常プレゼンテーション、または母体因子（弱い収縮）に克服できない病態で生じる。初期筋層収縮が第1産仔を骨盤管に移動させようとする。閉塞または収縮不十分が>4-6時間続くと持続的テタヌス収縮から子宮虚血発生。長期分娩（総>12時間）は母体低酸素血症/酸血症、胎児低酸素血症（臍帯圧迫/臍帯脱出の胎盤不全）、子宮破裂、出血を起こす。ハムスターでは難産が敗血性腹膜炎/ショックに急速進行（細菌易位と小体サイズ）。",
        "treatment": "Emergency management: 1) Stabilization: Keep female warm (37-38°C), IV/SC fluids (lactated Ringer's 50-100 mL/kg if needed—SC route often used in hamsters), oxygen if respiratory distress. 2) Medical management (successful if obstruction ruled out): Calcium gluconate 10% 50-100 mg/kg SC (calcium is often limiting in dystocia), wait 15-30 min for effect. Oxytocin 0.2-1.0 IU/kg SC/IM single dose, may repeat once at 15-30 min intervals (max 2 doses total). Monitor for pup delivery. 3) Surgical management (if unresponsive within 1-2 hours or obstruction confirmed): Emergency cesarean section under isoflurane inhalation anesthesia (small hamsters very sensitive; avoid injectable anesthetics if possible). Approach: low midline incision, exteriorize uterus, open at antimesentric border, remove all pups carefully. Uterotomy closure: 5-0 or 6-0 absorbable suture in simple interrupted pattern. Abdominal wall: 4-0 or 5-0 absorbable in simple interrupted. Skin: 4-0 non-absorbable suture or tissue adhesive. 4) Post-operative: Pain management critical—meloxicam 0.1-0.3 mg/kg SC q12h × 3-5 days (limit duration due to GI ulcer risk in hamsters), keep female and pups warm (37-38°C), allow nursing if pups viable, provide soft food/water, monitor for infection. 5) Antibiotics if infection risk: enrofloxacin 2.5-5 mg/kg SC/IM q12h × 10 days.",
        "treatment_ja": "ハムスターの難産緊急管理：1) 安定化：雌を温かく保つ（37-38℃）、輸液（乳酸リンガー50-100 mL/kg SC経路がハムスター推奨）、呼吸窮迫時酸素。2) 医学的管理（閉塞除外時成功）：グルコン酸カルシウム10% 50-100 mg/kg SC（難産でカルシウム制限的）、15-30分で効果待機。オキシトシン0.2-1.0 IU/kg SC/IM 1回、15-30分間隔で1回繰返（最大2回）。産仔分娩監視。3) 外科管理（1-2時間無反応または閉塞確認時）：イソフルラン麻酔下緊急帝王切開（ハムスター麻酔感受性高い；注射薬回避）。経路：下腹部正中切開、子宮外転、反中間膜部を開く、産仔慎重に除去。子宮縫合：5-0または6-0吸収性糸で単純割符。腹壁：4-0または5-0吸収性。皮膚：4-0非吸収性または接着剤。4) 術後：疼痛管理重要—メロキシカム0.1-0.3 mg/kg SC q12h × 3-5日（GI潰瘍リスク、期間限定）、雌と産仔を温かく（37-38℃）、産仔が生存していれば授乳を許可、軟食/水提供、感染監視。5) 感染リスク時抗菌薬：エンロフロキサシン2.5-5 mg/kg SC/IM q12h × 10日。",
        "prevention": "Prevention includes: breeding only females 6-8 months old (not older—dystocia risk increases exponentially after 10 months), ensuring good nutrition (especially calcium—critical for myometrial contractility), maintaining ideal body weight (avoid obesity), providing adequate nesting material (improves laboring comfort/success), maintaining optimal temperature (35-37°C), limiting litter size if possible (separate pups after weaning to reduce selection pressure for large offspring), regular breeding interval with adequate rest periods between litters.",
        "prevention_ja": "ハムスターの難産予防：6-8ヶ月齢の雌のみ育種（>10ヶ月で難産リスク指数関数的上昇）。栄養確保（特にカルシウム—筋層収縮に重要）、理想体重維持（肥満回避）、十分な産巣材提供（陣痛快適性向上）、至適温度維持（35-37℃）、可能ならば産仔数制限（離乳後産仔分離で大型産仔選抜圧軽減）、産仔間十分な休止期を伴う定期育種。",
        "prognosis": "Guarded. With early medical intervention (oxytocin + calcium), 40-60% of dystocias resolve without surgery. With emergency cesarean section, maternal survival 70-85% if performed within 1-2 hours of dystocia onset. Delayed surgery (>4-6 hours) or uterine rupture: mortality >80%. Pup survival depends on delivery timing (pups delivered vaginally typically have better viability than C-section pups in hamsters). Post-operative infection/peritonitis carries high mortality due to small body size and rapid systemic compromise.",
        "prognosis_ja": "ハムスターの難産予後：慎重。早期医学的介入（オキシトシン＋カルシウム）で40-60%難産は手術なしで解決。緊急帝王切開で難産発症から1-2時間以内で母体生存率70-85%。遅延手術（>4-6時間）または子宮破裂：死亡率>80%。産仔生存は分娩タイミング依存（膣分娩産仔は帝王切開より生存性良い）。術後感染/腹膜炎は小体サイズと急速全身障害で高死亡率。",
        "onset_pattern": {"acute"},
        "age_predisposition": {"adult", "young", "senior"},
    },
    {
        "name": "Mastitis",
        "name_ja": "乳腺炎",
        "symptoms": {"mammary_swelling", "mammary_redness", "fever", "appetite_loss", "lethargy"},
        "description": "Mastitis is a bacterial infection of the mammary gland in lactating females, causing systemic illness if untreated.",
        "description_ja": "授乳中のメスの乳腺感染。",
        "urgency": "high",
        "recommended_tests": ["physical_exam", "bacterial_culture", "CBC"],
        "causes": "Caused by: 1) Bacterial infection: Staphylococcus spp. (most common), Streptococcus spp., Escherichia coli; 2) Route of infection: damaged nipple tissue (trauma from pup biting, rough bedding), ascending infection from perineum, hematogenous spread; 3) Risk factors: poor cage hygiene, dirty/damp bedding, inadequate nutrition (especially vitamin A/E deficiency impairs immune function), large litter size (increased pup trauma), concurrent illness/immunosuppression.",
        "causes_ja": "ハムスターの乳腺炎の原因：細菌感染（Staphylococcus最多、Streptococcus、E. coli）。感染経路：乳頭損傷（産仔咬傷、粗い床材）、会陰部からの上行感染、菌血症。リスク因子：不良な飼育環境衛生、汚れた/湿った床材、栄養不足（ビタミンA/E欠乏で免疫障害）、大産仔数（産仔外傷増加）、並存疾患/免疫抑制。",
        "pathophysiology": "Mastitis develops when bacteria colonize the mammary gland epithelium, triggering acute inflammatory response. Bacterial toxins cause tissue damage and recruit neutrophils/macrophages. Inflammation causes: glandular swelling, congestion, edema, abscess formation. Lacteal stasis may occur from pain/swelling, leading to secondary milk cake formation. Systemic absorption of bacterial endotoxins and inflammatory mediators causes fever, anorexia, lethargy. In hamsters, small body size permits rapid sepsis progression; untreated mastitis can lead to mammary abscess, septicemia, and maternal death within 3-7 days. Infected milk may be ingested by nursing pups, causing GI infection/diarrhea.",
        "pathophysiology_ja": "乳腺炎は細菌が乳腺上皮にコロニー化し急性炎症反応を引き起こす。細菌毒素で組織損傷→好中球/マクロファージ募集。乳腺腫脹、充血、浮腫、膿瘍形成。乳汁停滞が痛み/腫脹で生じ、二次的milk cake形成。細菌エンドトキシン/炎症メディエーターの全身吸収で発熱、食欲不振、沈鬱。ハムスター小体サイズで敗血症が急速進行；未治療乳腺炎は乳腺膿瘍→敗血症→母体死亡（3-7日）。感染乳が授乳産仔に摂取→GI感染/下痢。",
        "treatment": "Immediate intervention critical: 1) Antibiotics empirically (culture pending): Enrofloxacin 10 mg/kg PO/SC q12h OR trimethoprim-sulfamethoxazole (TMS) 30 mg/kg PO q12h × 10-14 days. Once culture results available, switch to sensitivity-directed antibiotic. 2) Supportive care: SC/IP fluids (lactated Ringer's 50 mL/kg/day if dehydrated), pain management essential—meloxicam 0.1-0.3 mg/kg SC q12h × 5-7 days (avoid oral meloxicam as hamsters may not eat). 3) Local management: Warm (not hot) compresses q6-8h to affected glands (10-15 min, promotes blood flow), gentle milking if not too painful (may help drain infected fluid). 4) Nursing management: If pups young (<7 days), consider supplemental bottle-feeding with formula (hamster pups start eating solids around day 7); if older pups, they can be weaned earlier (day 15-18 vs normal 21 days). Infected milk is a concern; monitor pups for diarrhea. 5) Surgery if indicated: Mammary abscess drainage/lancing if abscess identified; rarely, partial mastectomy if gland is necrotic/irreversibly damaged. 6) Monitor for complications: Sepsis (high fever, lethargy, shock), secondary infections. Hospitalization recommended for first 48-72h of treatment if severely ill.",
        "treatment_ja": "ハムスター乳腺炎：迅速介入重要：1) 抗菌薬経験的（培養待機）：エンロフロキサシン10 mg/kg PO/SC q12h または TMS 30 mg/kg PO q12h × 10-14日。培養結果で感受性指向性抗菌薬に変更。2) 支持療法：輸液（乳酸リンガー50 mL/kg/日 脱水時）、鎮痛管理重要—メロキシカム0.1-0.3 mg/kg SC q12h × 5-7日（経口メロキシカムは採食低下）。3) 局所管理：温湿布（熱くない）q6-8h（10-15分、血流促進）、痛みが少ないなら温和な搾乳。4) 授乳管理：産仔<7日齢なら補助ボトル給餌考慮（ハムスター産仔は7日齢で離乳食開始）；>7日齢なら早期離乳（21日→15-18日）可能。感染乳が懸念；産仔下痢監視。5) 外科：乳腺膿瘍排膿/穿刺；稀に部分乳腺摘出（壊死/不可逆損傷）。6) 合併症監視：敗血症（高熱、沈鬱、ショック）、二次感染。重症なら最初48-72時間入院推奨。",
        "prevention": "Prevention includes: 1) Hygienic breeding: clean dry bedding (replace daily), remove soiled nesting material, sanitize cages regularly; 2) Nutritional support during lactation (increased caloric/nutrient demand): provide high-quality diet, extra protein (dog/cat food supplement), vitamin A/E supplementation; 3) Minimize nipple trauma: avoid rough bedding (aspen, cedar avoid as toxic), use soft paper bedding; 4) Litter size management: limit to 8-10 pups maximum (natural separation if possible to reduce pup density); 5) Maternal health: ensure adequate rest between litters (minimum 2-week interval), prevent obesity (increases infection risk), regular monitoring during lactation period. 6) Prompt treatment of any injury/illness in breeding female to prevent immunosuppression.",
        "prevention_ja": "ハムスター乳腺炎予防：1) 衛生的育種：清潔な乾燥床材（毎日交換）、汚れた産巣材除去、ケージ定期消毒。2) 授乳期栄養補給（増加カロリー/栄養要求）：高品質食、追加蛋白（犬/猫食補助）、ビタミンA/E補充。3) 乳頭外傷最小化：粗い床材回避（アスペン、スギは毒性）、軟紙製床材使用。4) 産仔数管理：最大8-10頭（可能なら自然分離で産仔密度軽減）。5) 母体健康：産仔間十分な休止（最小2週間）、肥満防止（感染リスク増）、授乳期間定期監視。6) 育種雌の損傷/疾患の迅速治療（免疫抑制予防）。",
        "prognosis": "Good with early aggressive treatment. With antibiotics started within 24-48h of symptoms, cure rate is 80-90%. Delayed treatment (>3-5 days) or sepsis development: mortality 40-60%. Mammary abscess or septicemia requires surgery and intensive care; mortality higher (50-70%). Surviving females may have permanent mammary damage/scarring, making future lactation problematic. Recommendation: spay females after weaning to prevent recurrence.",
        "prognosis_ja": "ハムスター乳腺炎の予後：早期積極的治療で良好。症状発症24-48時間以内に抗菌薬開始で治癒率80-90%。遅延治療（>3-5日）または敗血症発症：死亡率40-60%。乳腺膿瘍または敗血症は外科と集中治療で死亡率高い（50-70%）。生存メスは永続的乳腺損傷/瘢痕化で今後授乳困難。推奨：離乳後避妊手術で再発防止。",
        "onset_pattern": {"acute", "subacute"},
        "age_predisposition": {"adult", "young", "senior"},
    },
