    {
        "name": "Wet Tail - Chronic Form",
        "name_ja": "ウェットテイル（慢性型）",
        "symptoms": {"wet_tail", "weight_loss", "rough_coat", "diarrhea", "dehydration"},
        "description": "Wet Tail - Chronic Form is a clinical condition requiring veterinary evaluation, diagnosis, and appropriate treatment.",
        "description_ja": "慢性増殖性回腸炎により持続的な体重減少と間欠性下痢を引き起こす。",
        "urgency": "moderate",
        "recommended_tests": ["fecal_exam", "bacterial_culture", "radiography"],
        "causes": "Caused by chronic proliferative ileitis from persistent Lawsonia intracellularis infection, resulting in ongoing weight loss and intermittent diarrhea.",
        "causes_ja": "ハムスターにおけるウェットテイル（慢性型）の原因: 慢性増殖性回腸炎により持続的な体重減少と間欠性下痢を引き起こす。",
        "pathophysiology": "The pathological process involves tissue injury, inflammatory response, and progressive functional impairment. Without intervention, compensatory mechanisms may be overwhelmed, leading to clinical deterioration.",
        "pathophysiology_ja": "ウェットテイル（慢性型）はハムスターにおける細菌感染症である。病原菌は付着因子を通じて組織にコロニーを形成し、毒素産生、酵素分泌、免疫回避戦略などの病原性メカニズムを介して侵入する。好中球浸潤、サイトカイン放出、補体活性化を含む炎症カスケードが生じる。組織損傷は細菌の直接作用と宿主の炎症反応の両方に起因する。菌種と宿主の免疫状態に応じて、膿瘍形成、敗血症、または慢性肉芽腫性炎症が発生しうる。",
        "treatment": "Chronic wet tail is distinct from the acute form — caused by chronic proliferative ileitis (CPI) from persistent Lawsonia intracellularis infection of the ileal mucosa. Seen in hamsters that survived the acute phase or with low-grade chronic infection. Clinical signs: intermittent soft stool/diarrhea (not the profuse watery diarrhea of acute wet tail), progressive weight loss despite adequate appetite, rough coat, mild-moderate dehydration, thickened intestinal loops palpable on abdominal examination. May also see rectal prolapse from chronic straining. Diagnosis: clinical signs + history of prior wet tail episode or weaning-age onset. Fecal PCR for Lawsonia intracellularis (most specific). Fecal Gram stain may show characteristic intracellular silver-staining organisms (Warthin-Starry stain on biopsy is definitive). Abdominal radiograph/ultrasound: thickened ileal wall, possible ileal stricture from chronic inflammation. TREATMENT: chloramphenicol 50 mg/kg PO q12h × 14-21 days — historically most effective antibiotic for Lawsonia in hamsters. Alternative (due to chloramphenicol availability/handler risk): enrofloxacin 5-10 mg/kg PO q12h × 14-21 days + metronidazole 20 mg/kg PO q12h × 14 days (anti-anaerobic activity). Doxycycline 2.5-5 mg/kg PO q12h × 14-21 days is another option (good intracellular penetration). Nutritional support: high-calorie, easily digestible diet — Critical Care for Herbivores, baby food (meat-based), scrambled egg. Small frequent meals. Probiotics (Lactobacillus, Saccharomyces) may help restore gut flora — anecdotal evidence but commonly used. Fluid therapy: SC warm LRS 10-20 mL q12-24h for dehydration correction and maintenance. Rectal prolapse: if viable tissue, clean with warm saline + sugar to reduce edema, gently reduce with lubricated cotton-tipped applicator, purse-string suture (4-0 nylon) around anus leaving enough opening for defecation — remove in 3-5 days. If prolapse is necrotic or recurrent: colopexy under isoflurane anesthesia. Ileal stricture (late complication): may require surgical resection/anastomosis — very high-risk in hamsters. Pain management: meloxicam 0.2 mg/kg PO q24h for GI inflammation. Monitor body weight weekly — failure to gain weight despite treatment warrants reassessment. References: Jacoby (2007) Lawsonia in hamsters, Percy & Barthold (2007), Harkness & Wagner (1995).",
        "treatment_ja": "慢性型ウェットテイルは急性型とは異なり、回腸粘膜のLawsonia intracellularis持続感染による慢性増殖性回腸炎（CPI）が原因。急性期を生存した個体または低グレード慢性感染で見られる。臨床徴候: 間欠性軟便/下痢（急性型の大量水様下痢ではない）、十分な食欲にもかかわらず進行性体重減少、粗い被毛、軽度〜中等度脱水、腹部触診で肥厚した腸管ループ触知。慢性怒責による直腸脱の可能性。【診断】臨床徴候＋過去のウェットテイル歴または離乳期発症歴。Lawsonia intracellularisの糞便PCR（最も特異的）。糞便グラム染色で特徴的細胞内銀染色菌体（生検のWarthin-Starry染色が確定的）。腹部X線/超音波: 回腸壁肥厚、慢性炎症による回腸狭窄の可能性。【治療】クロラムフェニコール50mg/kg PO q12h×14-21日——ハムスターのLawsoniaに歴史的に最も有効。代替（クロラムフェニコールの入手性/取扱者リスクのため）: エンロフロキサシン5-10mg/kg PO q12h×14-21日＋メトロニダゾール20mg/kg PO q12h×14日（抗嫌気性活性）。ドキシサイクリン2.5-5mg/kg PO q12h×14-21日も選択肢（良好な細胞内移行）。栄養支持: 高カロリー・易消化食——Critical Care、ベビーフード（肉系）、スクランブルエッグ。少量頻回給餌。プロバイオティクス（ラクトバチルス、サッカロマイセス）で腸内フローラ回復に寄与の可能性——エビデンスは逸話的だが一般的に使用。輸液: SC温LRS 10-20mL q12-24h。直腸脱: 組織生存可能なら温生食＋砂糖で浮腫軽減、潤滑剤付き綿棒で優しく整復、肛門周囲巾着縫合（4-0ナイロン）で排便可能な開口を残す——3-5日後抜糸。壊死/再発性なら結腸固定術。回腸狭窄（晩期合併症）: 外科的切除/吻合が必要だがハムスターでは極めて高リスク。鎮痛: メロキシカム0.2mg/kg PO q24h（消化管炎症）。毎週体重モニタ——治療にもかかわらず体重増加不良は再評価。参考文献: Jacoby (2007), Percy & Barthold (2007), Harkness & Wagner (1995)。",
        "prevention": "Minimize stress during weaning (3-4 weeks) — this is the highest risk period for Lawsonia infection. Avoid overcrowding, sudden diet changes, and temperature fluctuations. Maintain strict cage hygiene. Quarantine new animals. There is no vaccine available. Acute wet tail survivors should be monitored long-term for chronic form development.",
        "prevention_ja": "離乳期（3-4週齢）のストレス最小化——Lawsonia感染の最高リスク期。過密・急な食事変更・温度変動を避ける。厳格なケージ衛生維持。新規動物の検疫。ワクチンはない。急性ウェットテイル生存個体は慢性型発症の長期モニタリング。",
        "prognosis": "Guarded — chronic proliferative ileitis is difficult to fully eradicate. Some hamsters stabilize with prolonged antibiotic therapy and nutritional support. Ileal stricture is a serious late complication that significantly worsens prognosis. Progressive weight loss despite treatment: poor. Given hamster lifespan (2-3 years), long-term management may constitute a significant portion of remaining life.",
        "prognosis_ja": "要注意——慢性増殖性回腸炎の完全根絶は困難。長期抗菌薬治療と栄養支持で安定化するハムスターもいる。回腸狭窄は予後を著しく悪化させる重大な晩期合併症。治療にもかかわらず進行性体重減少: 不良。ハムスター寿命（2-3年）を考慮すると長期管理は残存寿命の相当部分を占める可能性。",
        "onset_pattern": {"chronic"},
        "age_predisposition": {"young"},
    },
